# social-to-mealie's API keys and models. Copy to social-to-mealie.env and restrict it
# (cp social-to-mealie.env.example social-to-mealie.env && chmod 600 social-to-mealie.env); social-to-mealie.env is
# gitignored. It reads these only from its environment. Without the file it starts, but every import fails.
#
# Both keys are secrets: anyone who can reach social-to-mealie can use them (it has no login), so keep it on the LAN.

# An OpenAI API key (docs/installing.md#social-to-mealie). Give it a spending limit: every import costs a little.
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# A Mealie API token, made in Mealie under the user's profile (API tokens). Use a user of its own, not an
# administrator: the recipes it imports belong to that user, and the token can do whatever that user can.
MEALIE_API_KEY=ey...

# The models: one that turns speech into text, and a chat model with structured outputs that writes the recipe.
TRANSCRIPTION_MODEL=whisper-1
TEXT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
